## Terminology Standards

### Component Terms
- **Component**: React functional component with TypeScript interfaces
- **Element**: HTML element with semantic meaning
- **Hook**: Custom React hook following naming conventions
- **Pattern**: Reusable code structure with established conventions

### State Terms
- **Local State**: Component-level state using useState/useReducer
- **Global State**: Application-wide state using Context/Zustand
- **Server State**: Data from external sources with caching
- **Form State**: Form-specific state management with validation

### Styling Terms
- **CSS Module**: Scoped CSS file with component-specific styles
- **Custom Property**: CSS variable for consistent design tokens
- **Breakpoint**: Responsive design threshold for layout changes
- **Touch Target**: Minimum interactive element size (44px)

## Project Overview
This is a Vite + React + TypeScript website for Broken Loop Brewing, a craft brewery. The project uses CSS Modules, React Router, Framer Motion, and follows modern web development best practices.

## Technology Stack
- **Framework**: React 19.1.0 with TypeScript 5.8.3
- **Build Tool**: Vite 6.3.5
- **Styling**: CSS Modules with CSS Custom Properties
- **Routing**: React Router DOM 7.6.2
- **Icons**: Phosphor Icons
- **Animations**: Framer Motion
- **Content**: Markdown files with gray-matter frontmatter
- **Deployment**: Vercel with analytics

## AI Assistant Instructions

### Response Format
- Provide complete, working code solutions
- Include all necessary imports and dependencies
- Explain complex decisions with inline comments
- Show before/after examples for refactoring
- Always validate against existing project patterns

### Code Generation Preferences
- Prioritize TypeScript safety over convenience
- Use existing project utilities and hooks when possible
- Maintain consistency with established patterns
- Include error handling in all suggestions
- Test edge cases in proposed solutions

### Context Awareness
- Reference specific files when making suggestions
- Maintain awareness of component hierarchies
- Consider performance implications of suggestions
- Respect existing architecture decisions
- Flag potential breaking changes

## Decision Trees & Context Awareness

### When to Create New Components vs Modify Existing
```mermaid
graph TD
    A[New Feature Request] --> B{Similar component exists?}
    B -->|Yes| C{Can be extended with props?}
    B -->|No| D[Create new component]
    C -->|Yes| E[Add props to existing]
    C -->|No| F{Shared logic > 70%?}
    F -->|Yes| G[Extract common base component]
    F -->|No| D
```

### Component Complexity Guidelines
- **Simple** (< 50 lines): Single responsibility, minimal state
- **Medium** (50-150 lines): Multiple related responsibilities, local state
- **Complex** (> 150 lines): Consider splitting or using composition

### State Management Decision Matrix
| Scope | Complexity | Frequency | Solution |
|-------|------------|-----------|----------|
| Local | Low | Low | useState |
| Local | High | High | useReducer |
| Cross-component | Medium | Medium | Context |
| Global | High | High | Zustand/Redux |
| Server | Any | Any | React Query |

## Code Style & Formatting

### TypeScript Configuration
- Use strict TypeScript settings configured in `tsconfig.app.json`:
  ```json
  {
    "strict": true,
    "noUnusedLocals": true,
    "noUnusedParameters": true,
    "noFallthroughCasesInSwitch": true,
    "noUncheckedSideEffectImports": true,
    "verbatimModuleSyntax": true,
    "allowImportingTsExtensions": true,
    "target": "ES2020",
    "lib": ["ES2020", "DOM", "DOM.Iterable"]
  }
  ```
- All TypeScript errors must be resolved before committing
- Use `satisfies` operator for runtime type checking: `const config = { apiUrl: '...' } satisfies Config`
- Prefer branded types for domain safety: `type BeerId = string & { readonly __brand: unique symbol }`

### ESLint Rules
- Follow the existing ESLint configuration in eslint.config.js
- Use TypeScript ESLint recommended rules
- Enable React Hooks rules
- Use React Refresh plugin for development

### Prettier Configuration
- Line width: 80 characters
- Tab width: 2 spaces (no tabs)
- End of line: LF (Linux/Mac style)
- Prose wrap: Always for markdown files
- Format all supported files: JS, TS, JSON, MD, CSS

## Component Architecture

### File Structure
```
src/components/ComponentName/
├── ComponentName.tsx          # Main component
├── ComponentName.module.css   # CSS Module styles
├── ComponentName.d.ts         # TypeScript declarations
├── index.ts                   # Export file (optional)
└── README.md                  # Component documentation (optional)
```

### Comprehensive Component Template
```tsx
import React, { forwardRef } from 'react';
import styles from './ComponentName.module.css';
import { ComponentNameProps } from './ComponentName.d.ts';

/**
 * ComponentName - Brief description of component purpose
 * 
 * @example
 * <ComponentName variant="primary" size="large">Content</ComponentName>
 * 
 * @param variant - Visual variant of the component
 * @param size - Size variant of the component
 * @param children - Child elements to render
 * @param className - Additional CSS classes
 * @param onAction - Callback when action is triggered
 */
export const ComponentName = forwardRef<HTMLDivElement, ComponentNameProps>(({
  variant = 'default',
  size = 'medium',
  children,
  className = '',
  onAction,
  ...props
}, ref) => {
  // Memoized class names for performance
  const componentClasses = React.useMemo(() => {
    const baseClass = styles.component;
    const variantClass = styles[`component${variant.charAt(0).toUpperCase() + variant.slice(1)}`];
    const sizeClass = styles[`component${size.charAt(0).toUpperCase() + size.slice(1)}`];
    
    return [baseClass, variantClass, sizeClass, className].filter(Boolean).join(' ');
  }, [variant, size, className]);

  // Event handlers with error boundaries
  const handleAction = React.useCallback((event: React.MouseEvent) => {
    try {
      onAction?.(event);
    } catch (error) {
      console.error('ComponentName: Error in action handler:', error);
    }
  }, [onAction]);

  return (
    <div
      ref={ref}
      className={componentClasses}
      role={props.role || 'region'}
      aria-label={props['aria-label'] || 'Component description'}
      {...props}
      onClick={handleAction}
    >
      {children}
    </div>
  );
});

ComponentName.displayName = 'ComponentName';
```

### Hook Template
```tsx
import { useState, useCallback, useMemo } from 'react';

interface UseComponentNameOptions {
  initialValue?: string;
  onSuccess?: (value: string) => void;
  onError?: (error: Error) => void;
}

interface UseComponentNameReturn {
  value: string;
  setValue: (value: string) => void;
  loading: boolean;
  error: string | null;
  reset: () => void;
}

/**
 * useComponentName - Hook for managing component state
 * 
 * @param options - Configuration options for the hook
 * @returns Object containing state and actions
 */
export const useComponentName = (options: UseComponentNameOptions = {}): UseComponentNameReturn => {
  const { initialValue = '', onSuccess, onError } = options;
  
  const [value, setValue] = useState(initialValue);
  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(false);
  const [error, setError] = useState<string | null>(null);

  const isValid = useMemo(() => value.length > 0 && value.length <= 100, [value]);

  const reset = useCallback(() => {
    setValue(initialValue);
    setError(null);
    setLoading(false);
  }, [initialValue]);

  const setValueWithValidation = useCallback((newValue: string) => {
    try {
      setValue(newValue);
      setError(null);
      if (isValid) onSuccess?.(newValue);
    } catch (err) {
      const errorMessage = err instanceof Error ? err.message : 'Failed to set value';
      setError(errorMessage);
      onError?.(err instanceof Error ? err : new Error(errorMessage));
    }
  }, [isValid, onSuccess, onError]);

  return { value, setValue: setValueWithValidation, loading, error, reset };
};
```

## CSS Module Standards

### File Naming Conventions
- Component files: `ComponentName.tsx`
- CSS Module files: `ComponentName.module.css`
- TypeScript declarations: `ComponentName.d.ts`
- Global CSS files: `globals.css`, `variables.css` (in src/styles/)

### CSS Module Class Naming
- Use camelCase: `.headerRow`, `.beerCard`, `.sectionTitle`
- Be specific to the component: `.cardTitle` not `.title`
- Use semantic names: `.primaryButton` not `.blueButton`
- Follow BEM-like naming when appropriate: `.card`, `.cardTitle`, `.cardContent`

### CSS Module Import/Usage Pattern
```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT - CSS Modules
import styles from './Component.module.css';

export function Component({ variant = 'default' }) {
  const componentClass = variant === 'primary' 
    ? styles.componentPrimary 
    : styles.component;
    
  return (
    <div className={componentClass}>
      <h2 className={styles.title}>Title</h2>
      <div className={styles.content}>Content</div>
    </div>
  );
}

// ❌ INCORRECT - Global classes
export function Component() {
  return (
    <div className="component"> {/* ❌ Global class */}
      <h2 className="title">Title</h2> {/* ❌ Global class */}
    </div>
  );
}
```

