## Security Guidelines

### OWASP Top 10 Considerations

#### XSS Prevention
```typescript
// ✅ SAFE - Sanitize user input
import DOMPurify from 'dompurify';

const UserContent = ({ content }: { content: string }) => {
  const sanitizedContent = DOMPurify.sanitize(content);
  
  return (
    <div 
      dangerouslySetInnerHTML={{ __html: sanitizedContent }}
      className="user-content"
    />
  );
};

// ❌ UNSAFE - Direct user input
const UnsafeComponent = ({ content }: { content: string }) => {
  return (
    <div 
      dangerouslySetInnerHTML={{ __html: content }} // ❌ Vulnerable to XSS
    />
  );
};
```

#### Input Validation
```typescript
// ✅ SAFE - Validate all inputs
import { z } from 'zod';

const UserInputSchema = z.object({
  name: z.string().min(1).max(100),
  email: z.string().email(),
  age: z.number().min(18).max(120),
});

const validateUserInput = (data: unknown) => {
  try {
    return UserInputSchema.parse(data);
  } catch (error) {
    throw new Error('Invalid input data');
  }
};
```

#### CSRF Protection
```typescript
// ✅ SAFE - Include CSRF tokens
const submitForm = async (formData: FormData) => {
  const csrfToken = document.querySelector('meta[name="csrf-token"]')?.getAttribute('content');
  
  const response = await fetch('/api/submit', {
    method: 'POST',
    headers: {
      'Content-Type': 'application/json',
      'X-CSRF-Token': csrfToken || '',
    },
    body: JSON.stringify(Object.fromEntries(formData)),
  });
  
  return response.json();
};
```

### Secure Data Handling
```typescript
// ✅ SAFE - Never store sensitive data in localStorage
const useSecureStorage = () => {
  const storeSecureData = (key: string, data: any) => {
    // Use sessionStorage for temporary data only
    sessionStorage.setItem(key, JSON.stringify(data));
  };
  
  const getSecureData = (key: string) => {
    const data = sessionStorage.getItem(key);
    return data ? JSON.parse(data) : null;
  };
  
  const clearSecureData = (key: string) => {
    sessionStorage.removeItem(key);
  };
  
  return { storeSecureData, getSecureData, clearSecureData };
};
```

## Performance & Optimization

### React Performance Optimization
- Use `React.memo()` for expensive components that receive stable props
- Implement `useMemo()` for expensive calculations and object creation
- Use `useCallback()` for function props to prevent unnecessary re-renders
- Lazy load routes with `React.lazy()` and `Suspense`
- Avoid creating objects/arrays in render functions

### CSS Performance Optimization
- Use `will-change` sparingly and only for elements that will actually change
- Implement `contain` property for isolated components: `contain: layout style paint`
- Use `transform` and `opacity` for animations (GPU-accelerated)
- Avoid layout thrashing by batching DOM reads/writes with `requestAnimationFrame`
- Use `content-visibility: auto` for off-screen content

### Bundle Optimization
- Use dynamic imports for code splitting: `const Component = lazy(() => import('./Component'))`
- Minimize bundle size with tree shaking (ensure proper ES module exports)
- Use appropriate chunking strategies for SPA
- Implement route-based code splitting
- Use `webpack-bundle-analyzer` to identify large dependencies

### Core Web Vitals
- **LCP (Largest Contentful Paint)**: < 2.5s
- **FID (First Input Delay)**: < 100ms
- **CLS (Cumulative Layout Shift)**: < 0.1

### Performance Budgets
- **JavaScript bundle**: < 250KB gzipped
- **CSS bundle**: < 50KB gzipped
- **Time to Interactive**: < 3.5s on 3G
- **First Contentful Paint**: < 2s

### Project-Specific Performance Metrics
```typescript
// Performance budgets for Broken Loop Brewing website
const performanceBudgets = {
  // Bundle sizes
  js: { max: 250000, warn: 225000 }, // 250KB max, 225KB warning
  css: { max: 50000, warn: 45000 },  // 50KB max, 45KB warning
  
  // Core Web Vitals
  lcp: { max: 2500, warn: 2000 },    // Largest Contentful Paint (ms)
  fid: { max: 100, warn: 80 },       // First Input Delay (ms)
  cls: { max: 0.1, warn: 0.08 },     // Cumulative Layout Shift
  
  // Page load metrics
  fcp: { max: 2000, warn: 1500 },    // First Contentful Paint (ms)
  tti: { max: 3500, warn: 3000 },    // Time to Interactive (ms)
  
  // Image optimization
  imageMaxSize: { max: 500000, warn: 400000 }, // 500KB max image size
  
  // API response times
  apiResponse: { max: 1000, warn: 800 }, // 1s max API response
} as const;

// Usage in performance monitoring
const checkPerformanceBudget = (metric: keyof typeof performanceBudgets, value: number) => {
  const budget = performanceBudgets[metric];
  if (value > budget.max) {
    console.error(`Performance budget exceeded: ${metric} = ${value}`);
  } else if (value > budget.warn) {
    console.warn(`Performance budget warning: ${metric} = ${value}`);
  }
};
```

## Testing Strategy

### Unit Testing Patterns
```typescript
// Component testing with providers
const renderWithProviders = (
  ui: React.ReactElement,
  {
    preloadedState = {},
    ...renderOptions
  }: ExtendedRenderOptions = {}
) => {
  const Wrapper = ({ children }: { children: React.ReactNode }) => (
    <BrowserRouter>
      <ThemeProvider>
        <ErrorBoundary>
          {children}
        </ErrorBoundary>
      </ThemeProvider>
    </BrowserRouter>
  );
  
  return render(ui, { wrapper: Wrapper, ...renderOptions });
};

// Mock factories
const createMockBeer = (overrides: Partial<Beer> = {}): Beer => ({
  id: 'test-beer',
  name: 'Test Beer',
  abv: 5.0,
  ibu: 30,
  ...overrides,
});

// Component test example
describe('BeerCard', () => {
  it('renders beer information correctly', () => {
    const beer = createMockBeer({ name: 'Test IPA' });
    const { getByText } = renderWithProviders(<BeerCard beer={beer} />);
    
    expect(getByText('Test IPA')).toBeInTheDocument();
  });
  
  it('handles loading state', () => {
    const { getByTestId } = renderWithProviders(<BeerCard loading />);
    
    expect(getByTestId('loading-skeleton')).toBeInTheDocument();
  });
  
  it('handles error state', () => {
    const { getByText } = renderWithProviders(
      <BeerCard error="Failed to load beer" />
    );
    
    expect(getByText('Failed to load beer')).toBeInTheDocument();
  });
});
```

### Hook Testing
```typescript
// Hook testing with renderHook
import { renderHook, act } from '@testing-library/react';

describe('useBeers', () => {
  it('loads beers successfully', async () => {
    const { result } = renderHook(() => useBeers());
    
    expect(result.current.loading).toBe(true);
    
    await act(async () => {
      await result.current.reload();
    });
    
    expect(result.current.loading).toBe(false);
    expect(result.current.beers).toHaveLength(3);
  });
  
  it('handles errors gracefully', async () => {
    // Mock failed API call
    jest.spyOn(global, 'fetch').mockRejectedValueOnce(new Error('API Error'));
    
    const { result } = renderHook(() => useBeers());
    
    await act(async () => {
      await result.current.reload();
    });
    
    expect(result.current.error).toBe('Failed to load beers');
  });
});
```

### Integration Testing
```typescript
// Integration test example
describe('Beer List Flow', () => {
  it('allows user to filter and view beer details', async () => {
    const { getByPlaceholderText, getByText, findByText } = renderWithProviders(
      <BeerListPage />
    );
    
    // Filter beers
    const searchInput = getByPlaceholderText('Search beers...');
    fireEvent.change(searchInput, { target: { value: 'IPA' } });
    
    // Wait for filtered results
    const beerCard = await findByText('Hoppy Trails IPA');
    fireEvent.click(beerCard);
    
    // Verify navigation to detail page
    expect(getByText('Beer Details')).toBeInTheDocument();
  });
});
```

## Development Workflow

### Scripts
- `npm run dev`: Start development server with host binding
- `npm run build`: TypeScript build + Vite build
- `npm run lint`: ESLint checking
- `npm run format`: Prettier formatting
- `npm run format:check`: Check formatting without changes
- `npm run test`: Run unit tests
- `npm run test:coverage`: Run tests with coverage
- `npm run test:e2e`: Run end-to-end tests

### Git Workflow
- Feature branches: `feature/component-name`
- Commit format: `type(scope): description`
- Pre-commit hooks: lint, format, type-check
- Pull request template with checklist

### Code Review Checklist
- [ ] TypeScript strict mode compliance
- [ ] CSS Module naming conventions
- [ ] Accessibility requirements met
- [ ] Mobile responsiveness verified
- [ ] Performance impact assessed
- [ ] Error boundaries implemented
- [ ] Security considerations addressed
- [ ] Test coverage adequate

## Anti-Patterns to Avoid

### React Anti-Patterns
- **NEVER** use array indices as keys in lists
- **AVOID** mutating state directly
- **DON'T** create components inside other components
- **NEVER** use `useEffect` for derived state
- **AVOID** excessive prop drilling (use context after 3 levels)

### TypeScript Anti-Patterns
- **NEVER** use `any` type (use `unknown` if necessary)
- **AVOID** type assertions without proper checking
- **DON'T** ignore TypeScript errors with `@ts-ignore`
- **NEVER** use `Function` type (use proper function signatures)

### CSS Anti-Patterns
- **NEVER use `!important`** - it's considered an anti-pattern
- **AVOID** fixed pixel values for responsive design
- **DON'T** use deeply nested selectors (> 3 levels)
- **NEVER** use global CSS for component-specific styles
- Avoid inline styles

### Code Anti-Patterns
- Don't use emojis in code
- Avoid any types in TypeScript
- Don't ignore TypeScript errors
- Avoid prop drilling - use context or state management when needed

### Development Anti-Patterns
- Don't stop making changes and ask for permission before proceeding
- Avoid making multiple unrelated changes in one request
- Don't rely on past interactions without re-providing context
- Avoid vague error descriptions like "it's broken"

## Validation Rules

### Before Committing
- [ ] All TypeScript errors resolved
- [ ] ESLint passes without warnings
- [ ] Prettier formatting applied
- [ ] All imports are used
- [ ] CSS custom properties used correctly
- [ ] Mobile responsiveness verified
- [ ] Accessibility requirements met
- [ ] Security considerations addressed
- [ ] Test coverage adequate

### Code Quality Gates
- No `console.log` statements in production builds
- All functions have proper TypeScript types
- CSS classes follow naming conventions
- All images have proper alt text
- All interactive elements are keyboard accessible
- Error boundaries are implemented where needed
- Input validation is implemented
- XSS prevention measures are in place

## Documentation Standards
- Include JSDoc comments for complex functions
- Document component props with TypeScript interfaces
- Maintain README files for complex components
- Document any non-obvious implementation decisions
- Keep documentation up-to-date with code changes
- Use consistent terminology across all documentation
- Include examples for complex patterns
- Document breaking changes clearly

## Maintenance & Updates

### Rule File Updates
- Update frequency: Quarterly review and updates
- Change documentation: Document all rule changes with rationale
- Version tracking: Maintain changelog for rule updates
- Review cycles: Monthly review of rule effectiveness

### Cross-Reference Maintenance
- Verify all external rule file links are current
- Update cross-references when external files change
- Maintain consistency across all rule files
- Regular audit of rule file relationships

**Remember: This file serves as the single source of truth for development guidelines. Always reference external rule files for detailed patterns and maintain consistency across all development practices.** 